# Reusing VibeTrack Design Rules in Later Projects

## In this repo
Rules live at:
- `.cursor/rules/vibetrack-design-system.mdc` (always on)
- `.cursor/rules/vibetrack-ui-patterns.mdc` (when UI files are in context)

In Cursor chat, you can also `@`-mention a rule by name if needed.

## Option A — Copy into a new project (simplest)
1. Create the new project folder and open it in Cursor.
2. Copy this folder into the new project root:
   - from: `Decision-Helper-/.cursor/rules/`
   - to: `YourNewProject/.cursor/rules/`
3. Commit `.cursor/rules/` so teammates get the same guidance.
4. Tell the agent: "Follow the VibeTrack design system rules."

## Option B — User Rules (all your personal projects)
1. Open Cursor → **Customize → Rules** (or Cursor Settings → Rules).
2. Add a User Rule and paste the contents of `vibetrack-design-system.mdc` (body only is fine).
3. Those preferences then apply across projects on this machine.

## Option C — Remote / shared rules
1. Keep this repo (or a dedicated rules repo) on GitHub.
2. In Cursor: **Customize → Rules → Add Rule → Remote Rule (GitHub)**.
3. Point it at the repo that contains `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.
4. Cursor syncs imported rules for reuse.

## Prompt recipe for a new UI
Use a prompt like:

> Build a light minimalist page using the VibeTrack design system rules.
> Reuse Fraunces + Outfit, sage paper tokens, soft atmosphere gradients,
> centered 42rem column, no cards, quiet motion.

## Verify the agent is following the system
Checklist:
- Brand is large display type
- Background has soft sage atmosphere, not flat white
- Accent is sage green `#3f6f5a` (or token-based)
- No purple / dark-neon / terracotta defaults
- Sections are sparse and single-purpose
